    "long_instructions": "## Review `notnull()`\r\n\r\nIn Lesson 8, you used `notnull()` to check whether values are present. It returns `True` when a value is present and `False` when a value is missing.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nRun the program. The first condition filters for superheroes whose `Alias` ends with `\"r\"`.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nCompare the `Affiliation` column with the Boolean values returned by `notnull()`. Notice which values return `True` and which return `False`.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nModify the `notnull()` condition to check the `YearsActive` column instead of the `Affiliation` column. Run the program again.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nCompare the results. How did changing the column affect which superheroes appeared in the final DataFrame?\r\n:::",
    "ai_tutor_available": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
